hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another edition of modeling the masters  today we're gonna look at how a high  school jock whose only priority was  partying turn his life around to create  one of the most successful hotel chains  in the world this is the story of Izzy  Sharpe from the Four Seasons Hotel and  the top three lessons that you can learn  from his success  Izzy sharp is a Canadian businessman and  founder and chairman of Four Seasons  Hotel and Resorts sharp didn't have much  stability in his youth and move 15 times  in 16 years he also didn't care much for  school quoting the sharp my life in high  school revolved around sports partying  became my priority that all changed when  Sharpe was accepted into the  architecture program at Toronto's  Ryerson Polytechnical Institute he began  to earn high marks for his creations and  worked for his father building houses  and small apartment buildings yearning  for more at age 29 he founded the Four  Seasons Hotel in 1960 and opened his  first hotel on Jarvis Street in downtown  Toronto  he built a reputation for luxury and  sweating the details which allowed his  business of flourish in 2006 Bill Gates  and Prince Alwaleed bin Talal bought  control of the company for 3.4 billion  dollars  Sharp's current net worth is 540 million  dollars  by sweating the details and by reaching  for his dreams sharp turned his life  around and focused on business instead  of partying he was able to build one of  the most recognized companies in his  industry as a result to help you build  your business here are three action  items that you can learn from easy sharp  action item number one inspire your  employees if you ever want to build a  business beyond yourself you're gonna  have to have a team of people working  with you grow inspired to give their  very best every day sharp didn't become  the leading luxury hotel your in the  world all by himself in the over 50  years he's been in the industry sharp  has developed a unique leadership style  that has encourages employees to vote a  hundred and ten percent of themselves to  the company by creating a working  environment that is built on trust  credibility and integrity Sharpe has  inspired his team to work to realize  their best efforts in the end he  understood that this was a secret  ingredient to helping the company  realize its best results according to  Sharpe we do that first of all by  establishing a meaningful goal an  overriding purpose that most people can  relate to if the goal is clear and the  focus is sharp and constantly reinforced  we unify and energize through a sense of  common purpose and inspires employees to  art and effort action item number two  really service your customers the best  companies are based on happy customers  and repeat business you want to strive  to create an experience where customers  love buying from you and tell their  friends as well in each and every one of  its worldwide locations the Four Seasons  tends to set the top hotel price for the  area it's usually about twenty percent  higher than its closest competitor  how can sharp risks such as pricing  policy he does it by guaranteeing that  his guests get a fail-safe experience so  that a company's eager to pay the extra  fifty dollars to ensure a hassle-free  trip for an executive who might be  working on a 50 million dollar deal  according to sharp our competitors  interpreted luxury chiefly as dazzling  architecture and decor but how important  is that to our customers they're mostly  executives often under pressure  fighting jet lag stressed in the clock  we decided to redefine luxury  a service  action item number great live by the  golden rule the golden rule is to treat  people as you would like to be treated  it's not only a great way to achieve  happiness as an entrepreneur it's also a  highly profitable strategy driving force  behind sharp success has been his desire  to treat for seizes employees with the  same love of respect that they in turn  are expected to give their guests the  success of this policy has shown itself  not only in terms of customer happiness  but also employee engagement and  satisfaction for years the Four Seasons  has been the only Canadian company to  land on Fortune's magazine's list of the  best hundred companies to work for in  the US according to sharp we aim to  treat others as we would like to be  treated ourselves enforcing our credo  was the hardest part and senior managers  who couldn't or wouldn't live by a who  weeded out within a few years we hire  for attitude want people who like other  people and are therefore more motivated  to serve them compliments we can teach  attitude is ingrained so remember  inspire your employees really service  your customers and live by the golden  rule to finish up this video I wanted to  share one of my favorite true stories  about easysharp and some of his best  quotes in 1967 one Four Seasons employee  went to the extreme in demonstrating the  kind of service Sharpe was trying to  encourage a bellboy for the hotel Roy  diamond discovered that a dignitary  guest had left his briefcase behind  after checking out the guest soon called  from Washington stating that the  contents of the briefcase were essential  for an upcoming meeting feeling  responsible Diamond bought a plane  ticket at his own expense and personally  delivered the briefcase to the former  guests  thank you for joining me for another  edition of modeling the masters I hope  you enjoyed I'd love to hear your  thoughts and feedback if you want to  leave a comment below and please give  the video a thumbs up stay tuned for the  next episode
 

